<title>GREECE: IFC-SIGMA STOCK INDEX FUND COMES TO GREEK MARKET.</title>
<headline>IFC-SIGMA STOCK INDEX FUND COMES TO GREEK MARKET.</headline>
<dateline>ATHENS 1997-01-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>The International Finance Corporation (IFC) and Athens stock exchange member Sigma Securities along with Piraeus Bank Mutual Funds launched a new stock index fund based on IFC's investable index.</p>
<p>IFC's investable index for Greece includes 54 shares.</p>
<p>&quot;Greece has a 11.48 percent weighting in our investable index and institutional investors look at this number when making investment decisions,&quot; IFC head market analyst Costas Grigoriadis told a press conference.</p>
</text>
